# CraftAssay

Review contract: [`craftassay-review-spec-v1.1.md`](../../craftassay-review-spec-v1.1.md).
Architecture: [`docs/PHASE_1_BRIEF.md`](../../docs/PHASE_1_BRIEF.md).
If they drift on review behavior, the spec wins.

The name is CraftAssay. Familiar labels: Review, Findings, Scores,
Evidence, Compare versions. You may say what an assay is in ordinary
language: a test of composition and quality. Do not split the name
into two bold words. Do not tell the reader they can skip a word
in it. Do not lecture them on how to capitalize it.

The **skill** is the product. An agent reads it and writes each
review into a new dated folder under `<stem>.craftassay/`. npm
ships the folder. There is no command-line reviewer.

Canonical site host is craftassay.dev. craftassay.com is the same site.

Site and README speak as the product (CraftAssay / it). No corporate we.
No builder I. Oxford comma. No em dashes or semicolons in authored prose.

Do not invent scores. Use NR when evidence is missing. Do not implement
findings in the reviewed subject. CraftAssay may share first-use
evidence with Cold-eye. It does not issue a readiness verdict.
